## **3. Mathematical Theory of Engineering Search**

### **3.1 Effective Search Volume ($\Omega_{eff}$)**
$$ \Omega_{eff} = \{x \in \Omega : p_{eval}(x) > \epsilon\} $$
Where $p_{eval}(x)$ is the probability of evaluating candidate $x$. Intelligence ($I$) and Search Guidance ($V_{search}$) act to minimize $|\Omega_{eff}|$.

### **3.2 Search Guidance Quality ($V_{search}$)**
$V_{search}$ is the probability that the next evaluated candidate is closer to the optimum than random sampling:
$$ V_{search} = P\left(\frac{f(x_{t+1}) - f(x^*)}{f(x_t) - f(x^*)} < \frac{f(x_{rand}) - f(x^*)}{f(x_t) - f(x^*)}\right) $$
Increased by generative priors, physics-informed pruning, and multi-agent parallel exploration.

